WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.367
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.100
Thank you so much
for coming back on the show.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.534
-Oh, please, James Kanye Fallon,
we adore doing your show.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:09.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:11.934
You know, and so of all
the late night shows,

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.100
this is the easiest one
to fall asleep to.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.801
-Thank you so much.
-[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.701
-First of all, I think that
your comedy is just brilliant.

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.267
I do.
I was watching the monologue.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.367
To me, your comedy is
like crypto.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.601
I don't understand it,
but I admire it.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:29.601
But really, tell everyone what
you were -- what you were

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.434
telling about why it's finally
the right time

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.367
to suspend the Constitution.
What did that mean?

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:34.634
-[ Laughter ]
-I don't want to get into it.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.634
-Jimmy.
-Yeah?

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.334
-If Marty starts
humping your leg,

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:38.868
it's best to just let him
finish.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:39.667
-Oh.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.601
-It's gotten me through a lot of
flights and dinners,

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.267
I'll tell you that.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.767
-And all I got to say --
I know this is not right.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.567
First, I say, your beard --
I was going to make a little fun

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.667
of it because I thought at
first, it looked like, you know,

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.934
a COVID mask that they cut
a mouth hole in.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:01:00.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:02.367
I actually love the beard.
I really do.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.834
I miss the cold sore,
but I like the beard.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:06.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.200
-You miss the cold sore?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.167
-When I grow a beard, I look
like the guy in the Western

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:14.434
that goes, "Dag nab it."

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.033
-No, I'm not used to your beard.
It's kind of jarring in person.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.033
It's like seeing Steve
with a tan.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.100
You know, because --

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:26.467
Steve is whiter
than a Mormon golf team.

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:29.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.934
But you look great.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:34.300
You look like the offspring
if Santa had sex with an elf.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.501
-Oh, thank you so much.
-[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.567
-It makes you look like
a cool youth minister.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.934
-Oh, thank you.
-But honestly, I think you do

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.634
look like -- you look like you
bathed in testosterone.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.200
-Yeah, you do.
-And I'll tell you what.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.767
It's given you that buff
Marjorie Taylor Greene physique.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:52.801
-Thank you so much.
-Wow. What a compliment.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.400
-I'm excited that you guys
are -- you're hosting

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.133
"Saturday Night Live"
this weekend

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.067
with musical guest
Brandi Carlile.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.167
-That's right.
-That's right.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:01:59.534
-That's a big deal.
-Very big deal.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:02.234
-This is a big deal.
-She's a genius, you know.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.400
-And the truth,
we are very busy.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.734
But we always have time
to come down here

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.701
and do five to seven minutes
with you and...

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.601
...possibly ruin our careers

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:15.133
and destroy everything
that we built.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.467
-Well, it's appreciated.
-It's always a risk.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:19.133
But it is exc-- I mean,
I don't -- you know, Steve and I

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:22.601
think of ourselves as the Lennon
and McCartney of comedy.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.667
-Oh.
-No one else does, but we do.

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.133
-Oh, that's good.
-[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.300
Steve, are you going to play the
banjo on "Saturday Night Live"?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.767
-No, I'm not.
-You're not playing?

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:30.667
-No.
-Oh. Why not?

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.767
-I'll tell you why.
Because the cast voted.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.334
-I see, yeah.
-No, listen, when he pulls out

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:38.968
his banjo, people in China beg
for lockdowns.

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.033
-That's interesting.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:44.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.467
-Thank you so much.
Thank you.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:47.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.934
Thank you.

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:52.767
Oh, you're here.

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.467
I thought everyone
had wandered off.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:55.901
-I'm here too.
-I forgot.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:58.834
-You can't just put me down
and then ignore me.

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:01.968
-I want to say, I saw a very
funny promo that you guys did

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:03.901
for hosting
"Saturday Night Live" this week.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:06.400
It was so funny, I want to show
everyone here.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.701
Do you mind?
-Absolutely.

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:09.200
-That's what it's for.
-That's true. You're right.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.968
Here's Steve Martin
and Martin Short.

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:13.367
Here's the promo for "Saturday
Night Live" this weekend.

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:14.767
[ Elevator bell dings ]

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:20.033
♪♪

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:25.267
♪♪

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:31.734
[ Muffled groaning ]

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:34.434
-[ Gasps ] Water. I need water.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.467
[ Choking ]

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:43.033
-Hey. Hi.
It is such an honor.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.534
I'm so excited to meet you two.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:46.200
-Likewise, big fan.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.400
Ugh!

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.100
-I grew up watching your movies.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.467
The "Three Amigos!" and --

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:53.067
-Could you get me a green tea
with extra ice?

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.367
-Oh, I'm -- I'm actually one of
the cast members.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.634
-Oh! Oh, yeah.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.267
With a holiday cup?

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:00.667
-Holiday cup?

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:01.667
Got it.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:02.868
-Can't breathe.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:07.534
-Hi, I'm Martin Short,
and Steve and I are so excited

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:09.434
to be hosting
"Saturday Night Live" this week

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:11.067
with the great Brandi Carlile.

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.100
-Steve, got your green tea.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.367
-Aaah!
-Thanks.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.334
-Come on. That's how you do it.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.100
That is fantastic.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.300
-Thank you.
-That is so good.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.501
I loved it so much.
-Thank you.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:22.968
-I cannot wait for this weekend.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.434
Are you guys
in the holiday spirit?

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:25.968
-I am.
-I looked in the monitor,

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.901
and this is like
Margaret Hamilton wore these

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:29.334
in "The Wizard of Oz."
Look at that.

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:32.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.701
It's this thing.

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.133
-Yeah, I remember that.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:39.300
[ Laughter continues ]

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.400
Oh, my God.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.767
Auntie Em, Auntie Em.

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:43.868
-And I'll tell you
another thing.

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:44.934
Those aren't socks.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:46.067
-[ Laughter ]
-Oh, no. My gosh.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.834
-I have the worst rash. Yeah.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.434
-But I have noticed, actually,

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:51.567
that I find this so sweet
about New Yorkers.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:55.234
They take their mittens, and
they cut a hole in their mittens

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:57.033
so they can still give
each other the finger.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:00.901
-But it's difficult.
I mean, I never --

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:04.000
Steve and I are very close,
and I never know what to get you

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.234
for Christmas because of
the whole atheist thing.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:08.667
Although he's in the spirit.

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:10.701
He's already hung
his compression stockings

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.133
by the chimney with care.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:17.567
-I will say that my favorite
part of decorating the tree is

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:21.067
when at the end, I just put
a little tiny star on top.

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.734
And thank you for being up there
because --

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:28.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.000
I know that can get
uncomfortable.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.300
-Oh, my God.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.434
But, you know, office parties.

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:37.133
This is when STDs can be spread,
you know?

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.133
But I don't think of them
as a disease.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:40.601
I think of them as regifting.

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.467
And I love this -- when
New York -- when there's snows

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:46.567
in New York, the whole city

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.868
looks like Donald Trump Jr.'s
desk.

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:52.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:55.167
I did that for the band.
-Yes!

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.701
♪♪

00:05:57.701 --> 00:05:59.300
-You guys have such
a long history.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.300
You've worked professionally
together for --

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.601
-We have. And we have been
together so long,

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:07.234
we can actually finish
each other's careers.

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.968
-We're like the co-anchors
on "Good Morning America"

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:12.701
without the office sex,
you know.

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:13.767
-Yeah.

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:15.634
[ Audience oohs ]

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.334
-Are you still touring --

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:20.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.167
-Thank you!

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.868
Thank you.

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:26.067
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.067
Oh, you're still here?

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.367
-Yeah.
-Yes, we're all --

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:32.767
-I wish I had something
to bow for.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:35.601
-Are you still touring
with the show?

00:06:35.601 --> 00:06:36.901
Your show is called

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:38.701
"You Won't Believe What They
Look Like Today!"

00:06:38.701 --> 00:06:40.300
-Yes, that's true.
-Are you still touring?

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.701
-Well, it's fun --
-Yes.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.033
-It's fun.
I love touring with Steve.

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:46.801
But, you know, at his age,
there are certain problems.

00:06:46.801 --> 00:06:49.400
You know, I mean, when the
curtain goes up, Steve says,

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.934
"I'm ready, Jesus!"

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:53.067
And he starts heading
toward the light, you know?

00:06:53.067 --> 00:06:54.133
-Interesting.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:56.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:58.901
-[ Loudly ] I was telling people
how sometimes you get confused.

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:08.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:08.434 --> 00:07:10.434
-Steve!
-Yeah.

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:12.667
-We toured --
Right before COVID started,

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.667
we were touring Ireland.
-Oh, that's fun.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:19.100
-Yeah, but we had to leave
suddenly because [Laughs]

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:21.501
Marty couldn't say "air lingus"
without giggling.

00:07:21.501 --> 00:07:24.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:27.534
-You both got a bunch of things
going on.

00:07:27.534 --> 00:07:29.133
"Only Murders in the Building,"
come on.

00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:30.267
How great is that show?

00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:31.467
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-It is unbelievable.

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.534
-Thank you.
-TV at its finest.

00:07:33.534 --> 00:07:35.701
-Go ahead and bow.
-Yeah, now you got to bow.

00:07:35.701 --> 00:07:37.534
-Give them your bow.
-No, not like I'm not in it.

00:07:37.534 --> 00:07:40.601
-No, you co-created it
or created or whatever you did.

00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:43.100
You should take the bow.
It's true. It's his idea.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:44.267 --> 00:07:46.033
-That's a bow.
-Yeah.

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:47.567
-You're hosting
"Saturday Night Live" --

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.934
-I'm not going to bow like you
because I don't need to.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.100
-Wow!

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.801
[ Audience oohs ]

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:55.367
-Steve, you have this fantastic
memoir, by the way.

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:56.834
-Oh, thank you.
-Oh, look at that.

00:07:56.834 --> 00:07:58.934
-"Number One Is Walking."
Congratulations on this.

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:01.234
This is a fantastic memoir.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:01.234 --> 00:08:04.067
Memoirs, your time in movies.

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:06.968
Marty, you're in the "Beauty and
The Beast: 30th Anniversary."

00:08:06.968 --> 00:08:09.534
You are playing Lumiere.
-Lumiere.

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:11.000
[ French accent ]
Be our guest. Be our guest.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.667
This is our service
to the guest.

00:08:12.667 --> 00:08:14.400
[ Normal voice ] And of course,
the fabulous H.E.R.,

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.367
who will be out soon is Belle.

00:08:16.367 --> 00:08:17.534
She's Belle.

00:08:17.534 --> 00:08:19.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:19.634 --> 00:08:21.234
-You guys have
never been busier.

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:24.834
-Yes, we're busier than Nick
Cannon's child-support lawyer.

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:27.000
-[ Laughter and applause ]
-Congrats on everything.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.234
Steve Martin, Martin Short,
everybody.

00:08:29.234 --> 00:08:32.367
Catch them hosting "Saturday
Night Live" this weekend

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:34.400
with musical guest
Brandi Carlile.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:37.133
Steve, Martin, and I are playing
a fun game when we come back.

00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:38.133
Stick around.

